On the jetty
The joints of this rickety old jetty are becoming rotten and warped with constant lapping of the river water. The small boat is moored here by a rope off the east end of the jetty; westward is a tract of uncultivated land and to the southwest lies a field of golden wheat.
Your score just went up by 5 points.
>
Scrub
Here, bramble bushes and weeds that constantly tug and tear at your ankles have run amok. This type of foliage continues to the west and north but becomes stronger to the southwest, forming a copse. To the east is the rickety old jetty and a wheatfield lies to the south. Dragging an extremely heavy trunk is an frail old man, wearing a white sash.
